NAME
       printf - format and print data

SYNOPSIS
       printf format [arguments...]

DESCRIPTION
       Writes ARGUMENTS under the control of FORMAT. The format is
       reused from the beginning until every argument is consumed.

       Conversions: %s %d %i %u %x %X %o %c and %%.
       Escapes: \n \t \r \\ and \0NNN for an octal byte.

EXAMPLES
       printf '%s is %d years old\n' Cervus 1

SEE ALSO
       echo(1)
